barBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review advisory resolution and frozen test contract card:\n\n- Trigger: timing is armed when CI has a conventional truthy value or REBAR_FIXTURE_TIMING=1; otherwise it is silent. The threshold is 1.0 monotonic seconds.\n- Interception: the editor fixture wraps the exact ThreadingHTTPServer constructor, socketserver.TCPServer.server_bind, and socket.getfqdn callables only during edit_workflow setup, restoring each before the test body. This separates nested constructor, bind, and reverse-DNS spans while preserving arguments, return values, and exceptions.\n- Authoritative contract: the ticket acceptance criteria and operator requirement require attribution of any operation/test over 30 seconds without changing coverage or behavior.\n- Preconditions: deterministic fake monotonic readings cross 1.0s with timing armed; the focused editor fixture exercises the real edit_workflow path.\n- Test tier: in-process unit tests for threshold/env/emission and callable transparency, plus the existing focused real editor fixture path; a source-text assertion would not prove runtime attribution.\n- Observable postconditions: emitted records name worker, node, fixture/span, and elapsed seconds; unarmed and sub-threshold controls emit nothing; wrapped calls return the exact result and re-raise the exact exception.\n- Gate: the new observability test module and focused editor module run under the default pytest CI gate, followed by lint and typecheck.\n- Negative controls: unarmed timing and a 0.99s span remain silent.\n\nThe organic post-merge run remains the deliberate Stage-3 dynamic experiment and will be recorded before this investigation ticket closes.","timestamp":1786745695073958001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED/GREEN evidence before commit:\n\n- Final RED with no implementation: 8 failures. The root conftest tests failed because time/pytest_fixture_setup/_timed_ci_call did not exist; the editor wiring test failed because _instrument_editor_server_setup did not exist. A first oracle attempt imported tests/unit/conftest.py by accident; per the strict test-modification guard, I removed the implementation, corrected the test to obtain the already-loaded root plugin, and re-proved this final RED before reapplying the implementation.\n- GREEN: 9 focused observer/wiring/loopback tests passed, then both full focused modules passed (24 tests in 4.61s). The same 24 tests passed under xdist -n 2 with CI=true in 3.48s; all 24 nodes collect and execute without skip/xfail.\n- Mutation proof: changing the threshold from 1.0s to 999.0s returned test_fixture_setup_hook_reports_worker_node_fixture_and_elapsed to RED with DID NOT WARN; restoring 1.0s returned the suite to GREEN.\n- Gates: worktree-venv make lint passed (2023 files formatted, actionlint/zizmor/complexity/DCO checks clean); worktree-venv make typecheck passed across 541 source files.\n- Safety: timing is disabled outside CI/REBAR_FIXTURE_TIMING=1, uses only monotonic clock + pytest warnings, adds no dependency/external call, and restores the constructor/bind/getfqdn callables before each editor test body. Original return objects and exception identity are covered.","timestamp":1786746123321136001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed commit e88b8c6b83 to Gerrit change 1793 without waiting for a non-contentious window. The new Verified run is 31846417650, created 2026-08-14T22:23:22Z. Local review-code was unavailable by configuration (verify.enable_code_review is off), so Gerrit LLM-Review remains the authoritative review. No further push will occur while this run is pending.","timestamp":1786746262852722001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase-1 RCA confirmed by Gerrit Verify run 31846417650 (macOS job 94913955831). Dynamic nested timing emitted `socket.getfqdn elapsed=35.013s`, `threading_http_server_constructor elapsed=35.014s`, and surrounding `_server fixture_setup elapsed=35.020s` for `test_server_binds_loopback_only`; TCP bind emitted nothing above the 1s threshold. This confirms CPython ThreadingHTTPServer construction synchronously performs reverse-DNS lookup of numeric loopback and rules out TCP bind, `_no_repo_commits`, tmp_path, and generic worker starvation for this recurring fixed ~35s phase. The overall run was 29m47s and macOS job 28m06s; default suite 23m25s and integration 2m38s. No other individual operation/test crossed 30s in the observed macOS default-tier timing. Defect legitimacy: defect/performance regression against the operator requirement that individual tests be negligible and CI average remain 20–30m without coverage loss. OSS precedent is strong: pip patches `socket.getfqdn` in its HTTP test server due to the same ~30s reverse-DNS delay; aiohttp and urllib3 bind literal loopback/raw sockets without this lookup. Observability change e88b8c6b83 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and merged as Gerrit 1793 at 2026-08-14T22:54:08Z. A separate RED/GREEN fix ticket will preserve literal-loopback server semantics while eliminating the irrelevant reverse lookup.","timestamp":1786748080150186001}],"created_at":1786745190464712001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"138c521b-34a6-442d-8102-c1810d34d5ab","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4f50-b1f2-78af-4326"},{"link_uuid":"fa514aa7-18e3-41a5-a2e4-b77546c3f59b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"09c6-c848-bafd-41ac"}],"description":"## Context\nThree genuine Gerrit Verify runs assign an almost identical setup duration to tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py::test_server_binds_loopback_only: 35.06s before static Pandoc replay and 35.09s in both post-static-corpus patch sets. Focused test/module runs are subsecond/2.44s; targeted editor setup instrumentation was below 4ms; a 10,000-directory APFS tmp_path benchmark stayed below 3.4ms. Recurrence after removing complete Pandoc subprocess replay rejects the prior generic worker-starvation account. CPython ThreadingHTTPServer construction synchronously calls socket.getfqdn(host), which performs reverse DNS even for numeric 127.0.0.1, making a fixed macOS resolver timeout the leading dynamic hypothesis. Existing pytest durations identify only the aggregate setup phase, so one organic CI observation needs nested timing before changing behavior.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a thresholded pytest fixture-setup observer that emits worker id, node id, fixture name, and monotonic elapsed time only for fixture spans above one second.\n- Add transparent, semantics-preserving timing around the editor server constructor, TCP bind, and socket.getfqdn call during the _server fixture; emit only spans above one second and preserve original arguments, return values, and exceptions.\n- Keep output quiet outside CI/explicit opt-in and avoid any new dependency or external call.\n- Prove locally that the observer names the correct nested span using deterministic delayed fakes, then run the focused editor and observability tests.\n- Land through Gerrit and use the first organic macOS/Ubuntu full-route run as the discriminating experiment. H1 predicts ~35s in getfqdn(127.0.0.1) on macOS with bind milliseconds; H2 predicts the inverse; H3 predicts the time belongs to _no_repo_commits rather than _server.\n- Record the confirmed mechanism and create a linked RED/GREEN fix ticket only after runtime evidence discriminates the hypotheses. Back out with a Gerrit revert if instrumentation changes test semantics or produces noisy routine logs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fixture spans above one second identify worker, node, fixture, and elapsed seconds.\n- [ ] Editor server setup separately measures constructor, TCP bind, and getfqdn without changing their behavior.\n- [ ] Instrumentation is silent below threshold and outside CI/explicit opt-in.\n- [ ] Deterministic tests prove each discriminating span is attributed correctly.\n- [ ] Focused editor tests and broader test-observability guards pass.\n- [ ] Lint, typecheck, action/workflow policy gates pass as applicable.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 are recorded before merge.\n- [ ] The first organic post-merge macOS/Ubuntu observation is recorded.\n- [ ] A confirmed root cause or explicit inconclusive experiment result is written back before close.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"Emit thresholded fixture-level CI timing with worker and node attribution."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py","reason":"Measure nested editor server constructor, TCP bind, and reverse-DNS spans without changing semantics."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_slow_fixture_observability.py","reason":"Prove thresholding, attribution, and opt-in behavior deterministically."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[["relates_to","09c6-c848-bafd-41ac"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cb0cd028-62d8-481f-bb77-a15b0d3746ab","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","observability","performance","macos"],"ticket_id":"9d6b-7628-7af9-4dcd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Instrument recurring 35-second macOS editor setup long pole","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f561a809-d9d3-4d7e-a2bf-e544749da9a7","72f0fc19-0870-4c39-bb1b-57af1d91a73f","138c521b-34a6-442d-8102-c1810d34d5ab","7a531884-ac4f-4f55-aeeb-538a8bf4910d","cb0cd028-62d8-481f-bb77-a15b0d3746ab","6715617b-2ccb-4567-b90f-f3217cac962d","960e99d5-8dda-4df2-869e-f0d6167376ee","1fbb8a30-9120-43ec-a57c-18c820685efa","fa514aa7-18e3-41a5-a2e4-b7754